<div id="omarchy" v-cloak>
  <div purpose="page-container">
    <div purpose="page-content">
      <div purpose="hero-and-top-section">
        <div purpose="page-hero">
          <div purpose="page-hero-content">
            <div purpose="page-hero-headings">
              <h1>Omakase for your desktop, full control for your fleet.</h1>
            </div>
            <div purpose="page-hero-text">
              <p>Manage Omarchy like you manage macOS and Windows. Give employees the distro they want without losing compliance and control.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="button-row" class="d-flex">
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
              <animated-arrow-button href="/pricing">View pricing</animated-arrow-button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="page-hero-image">
            <img alt="Omarchy managed by Fleet" src="/images/os-projector-omarchy-478x478@2x.png">
          </div>
        </div>

        <div purpose="quote-section">
          <p purpose="quote-text">"I’ve been recommending Fleet whenever I get the MDM question 🤘"</p>
          <div purpose="quote-author-info">
            <div purpose="quote-author-image">
              <img alt="DHH" src="/images/testimonial-author-dhh-48x48@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="name-and-title">
              <p purpose="author-name">DHH</p>
              <p purpose="author-title">Creator of Omarchy &bull; Ruby on Rails</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div purpose="top-section">
          <div purpose="page-section">
            <div purpose="banner">
              <div purpose="banner-text">
                <div purpose="banner-heading">
                  <h2>Linux support hasn't kept up with Linux adoption</h2>
                </div>
                <div purpose="banner-body">
                  <div purpose="banner-item">
                    <h5>No standard to enforce</h5>
                    <p>IT can't standardize configs across distros the way it can with macOS or Windows.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div purpose="banner-item">
                    <h5>One distro or none at all</h5>
                    <p>Most MDMs only support Ubuntu, leaving every other distro, including Omarchy, unmanaged.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div purpose="banner-item">
                    <h5>Growing faster than IT can track</h5>
                    <p>Desktop Linux passed 10% market share in 2026, up from 5% the year before, often arriving before IT has planned for it.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div purpose="banner-image"></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div purpose="page-section">
            <div purpose="section-heading">
              <h2>Built for Linux, backed by people who've done the work</h2>
            </div>
            <div purpose="three-column-list" class="sm-gap">
              <div purpose="feature">
                <div purpose="feature-title">
                  <h5>Omarchy included, not bolted on</h5>
                </div>
                <p>Fleet treats Omarchy as a first-class platform, alongside every other Linux distro your team runs.</p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="feature">
                <div purpose="feature-title">
                  <h5>Migrating doesn't mean stalling out</h5>
                </div>
                <p>Companies cut new-hire provisioning errors from 90% to under 1%, consolidating Mac, Linux, and Windows onto Fleet.</p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="feature">
                <div purpose="feature-title">
                  <h5>Open source</h5>
                </div>
                <p>Fleet's agent is open source, so Omarchy users can see exactly what's running on their device.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div purpose="distro-icons">
              <img alt="Omarchy logo" src="/images/os-icon-omarchy-40x40@2x.png">
              <img alt="Arch Linux logo" src="/images/os-icon-arch-linux-40x40@2x.png">
              <img alt="Ubuntu logo" src="/images/os-icon-ubuntu-40x40@2x.png">
              <img alt="Amazon Linux logo" src="/images/os-icon-amazon-linux-40x40@2x.png">
              <img alt="Red Hat Enterprise Linux logo" src="/images/os-icon-rhel-40x40@2x.png">
              <img alt="Fedora logo" src="/images/os-icon-fedora-40x40@2x.png">
              <img alt="CentOS logo" src="/images/os-icon-centos-40x40@2x.png">
              <img alt="openSUSE logo" src="/images/os-icon-opensuse-40x40@2x.png">
            </div>
          </div>

          <div purpose="quote-section">
            <p purpose="quote-text">"Fleet has explicit support for Omarchy. It’s a great option if your organization needs to manage Linux."</p>
            <div purpose="quote-author-info">
              <div purpose="quote-author-image">
                <img alt="DHH" src="/images/testimonial-author-dhh-48x48@2x.png">
              </div>
              <div purpose="name-and-title">
                <p purpose="author-name">DHH</p>
                <p purpose="author-title">Creator of Omarchy &bull; Ruby on Rails</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div purpose="features-section">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Getting SOC 2 does not mean giving up Linux" src="/images/get-soc-2-linux-600x338@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Getting SOC 2 &ne; giving up Linux</h5>
              <p>Use Fleet’s policy engine to enforce and monitor custom security checks on Omarchy, including SOC 2, ISO 27001, FedRAMP, BSI C5, SecNumCloud, G-Cloud, BIO, PCI, HIPAA, and CIS, NIST.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <div purpose="feature-image">
              <img alt="Offboard Linux users and stay compliant" src="/images/remote-lock-omarchy-600x338@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="image-caption">
              <h5>Offboard Linux users and stay compliant</h5>
              <p>Cut off access to cached credentials quickly when an employee leaves the company. Lock an Omarchy device the moment it goes missing or as part of an investigation. </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div>
        <div purpose="quote-and-logos">
          <div purpose="section-quote">
            <div purpose="quote-author-image">
              <img alt="Roger Cantrell" src="/images/testimonial-author-roger-cantrell-100x100@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="quote-content">
            <p purpose="quote-text">“We chose Fleet because they take Linux desktop management seriously. It was smooth as butter to set up and start deploying.”</p>
            <div purpose="quote-author-info">
              <div purpose="name-and-title">
                <p purpose="author-name">Roger Cantrell</p>
                <p purpose="author-title">IT Operations Engineer, Nutanix</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div purpose="logo-grid" class="d-none d-sm-flex">
            <div purpose="logo-row">
              <div purpose="logo" class="nutanix">
                <img alt="Nutanix logo" src="/images/logos/logo-nutanix-color-93x12@2x.png">
